  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-sonar",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nA compact, draggable deep-sea usage dashboard for the DeepSeek Harness Web UI.\n\n`dsh-sonar` adds a Fish-logo floating launcher without narrowing the conversation. Click the Fish to open a complete session dashboard; drag it anywhere in the viewport. The panel automatically chooses a direction where it fits, and `Escape` or another Fish click collapses it. While the model is answering, lightweight bubbles rise around the launcher.\n\nThe dashboard includes:"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-sonar",
      "text": "- a green / amber / red context-window gauge;\n- an accounted-token donut for uncached input, cache read/write, output, and reasoning when the installed Harness exposes it;\n- heuristic system prompt, tool schema, and conversation composition;\n- turn, step, model time, tool time, cache hit rate, and cumulative tokens;\n- exact DeepSeek `total_balance`, refreshed after each completed turn or manually."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-sonar",
      "text": "The API key stays on the Host. The browser calls a same-origin `dsh-sonar` route that returns only `{ totalBalance }`; cross-site and non-IP/localhost Host requests are rejected, and responses are never cached."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install from GitHub",
      "text": "The repository commits its built `lib/` artifacts, so a Git install does not need to execute a build script:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:Howe829/dsh-sonar#v0.1.0\ndsh --profile web\n```\n\nPin a release tag for repeatable installations. Remove it with:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-sonar\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "The bundle inserts one `dsh-sonar` row. Defaults use the managed `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` credential and the public DeepSeek API:\n\n```yaml\n- id: dsh-sonar\n  name: dsh-sonar\n  config:\n    apiKeyEnv: DEEPSEEK_API_KEY\n\nA later profile or home patch can replace this row. Harness patch configuration is row-replacing, so restate every field you want to keep."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install\npnpm run verify\npnpm pack --pack-destination .artifacts\n```\n\nThe current stable dsh-sonar release is [`v0.1.0`](https://github.com/Howe829/dsh-sonar/releases/tag/v0.1.0). It is tested against the public DeepSeek Harness `0.1.0-rc.6` package family. DeepSeek Harness itself remains a developer preview, so future Harness releases may require compatibility updates."
    },
    {
      "section": "Privacy and model impact",
      "text": "This is a read-only UI plugin. It adds no tools, prompts, commands, durable session events, or model-visible context. It does not alter the request envelope or KV cache behavior."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
